## Quick Reference

### Creating Documentation Checklist

- [ ] Determined appropriate category (learnings/planned/delivered/running)
- [ ] Checked if similar documentation exists
- [ ] Created file in correct subdirectory
- [ ] Used descriptive file name following conventions
- [ ] Added proper frontmatter (date, purpose, related)
- [ ] Considered if `CLAUDE.md` needs updating (for critical docs)
- [ ] If critical, added reference in `CLAUDE.md` with link

### Moving Existing Documentation

If you find documentation in the wrong location:
- [ ] Determine correct subdirectory
- [ ] Move file to correct location
- [ ] Update any references in `CLAUDE.md` or other docs
- [ ] Consider if file should be in root (only if essential reference)

