## Why This Rule Exists

**Benefits of proper documentation placement:**
- ✅ Easy to find relevant documentation
- ✅ Clear organization by purpose and status
- ✅ Maintains project structure
- ✅ Prevents documentation sprawl
- ✅ Makes it clear what's active vs completed
- ✅ Helps new team members navigate the project

**Problems without this rule:**
- ❌ Documentation scattered across the project
- ❌ Hard to find relevant information
- ❌ Duplicate or conflicting documentation
- ❌ Unclear project organization
- ❌ Difficult to maintain

---

## Quick Decision Tree

```
Is this documentation?
    │
    ├─ Yes → Is it essential quick reference?
    │   │
    │   ├─ Yes → Root of development_guidelines/ (rare)
    │   │
    │   └─ No → What is its status?
    │       │
    │       ├─ Bug fix / Troubleshooting / Guide → learnings/
    │       ├─ Planned / Future work → planned/
    │       ├─ Completed feature / Deliverable → delivered/
    │       └─ Active work in progress → running/
    │
    └─ No → Not documentation, place according to code organization rules
```

